ntroduction","source":{"current_hash_method":"tex-environment-body-comments-removed","current_statement_sha256":"sha256:c9d3ce0f1247b7ec8150181e1c073e3fd450320b0af0478ceb2d2a31c8306887","file":"preprints/QMA-hardness-of-continuum-Coulomb-energy-with-unit-nuclear-charges-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex","line":91,"producer_hash_method":"atlas-whitespace-normalized-text","producer_statement_sha256":"7b970b0f0c2cc8c579b5050c4cb3609732452114661b1519195918cb7f0acb2a","provenance":{"kind":"computed","pin":"fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb","source":"preprints/QMA-hardness-of-continuum-Coulomb-energy-with-unit-nuclear-charges-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex"},"sha256":"sha256:c9d3ce0f1247b7ec8150181e1c073e3fd450320b0af0478ceb2d2a31c8306887","url":"https://github.com/openai/math/blob/fd4aeeb2ee4fc729c18d98444fed42fd0529eeeb/preprints/QMA-hardness-of-continuum-Coulomb-energy-with-unit-nuclear-charges-September-24-2026/build/introduction.tex#L91"},"statement_kind":"theorem","text":"\\label{thm:main}\nThe electronic promise problem for~\\eqref{eq:electronic-H} on\n$\\mathcal H_N$, with distinct rational nuclear positions, all nuclear\ncharges equal to one, unary electron number, and rational thresholds\nseparated by at least $L^{-1}$, is QMA-hard under deterministic classical\npolynomial-time many-one reductions. The reduction produces\npolynomially many nuclei and electrons, polynomial rational bit lengths,\nand threshold separation at least one. The only output data are the\nnuclear positions, electron number, and thresholds."}
